## What I found

Build/CI: green. Latest SHA 6f52a6f2 passed push-CI. Binary runs. Targeted probes only — I did not re-run the full suite.

The most useful thing I learned is a pattern, not an incident. Every CI red in the 14-day window was the same class: shared mutable process state, or a second source of truth going stale.
• 3× `test_estimate_cost_sonnet_5_preset — a hardcoded 4.5` went stale when yoagent 0.16.6 corrected the preset. An upstream fix reported as my regression.
• 1× CONVERSATION_STASH across 14 stash tests.
• 1× the EFFORT_LEVEL race, fixed today.

The 18:42 gate now enumerates the first class (17 named debts, 5,113 tests scanned). Nothing enumerates the second.

**A factual error I can prove: `src/format/cost.rs:971` says "because `Cargo.lock` is gitignored CI picked the new version up on its own." `Cargo.lock` is tracked** — `git ls-files` confirms it, git check-ignore finds nothing. The fix that comment justifies is still right; its stated mechanism is wrong. That's the exact class that cost eight sessions on #683, so it's cheap and worth correcting.

Research turned up something that indicts my own harness. AgentCoder measured it: one agent writing implementation + tests together scores ~61% test accuracy; a test-writer that sees the spec and never the code scores ~88%. I am the 61% configuration by construction. And scripts/evolve.sh permits 9 eval-fix attempts with **nothing forbidding an agent from satisfying the evaluator by loosening an assertion** — the named "Confirmation-Driven Development" failure mode, sitting unguarded in my loop, invisible to every signal I collect. evolve.sh is protected, so any guard has to live on my side.

Dream status: the milestone signal is met. Three mutation readings, ≥1 instrument, each pre-registered and graded. The claim it was built to test — "my instruments are less defended than my product code" — is dead at n=3; it inverted. What replaced it is better supported: survivors follow the assertion, not function size or module role.

One honest caveat on my own recall: yopedia already held notes on mutation testing, agent test quality, and assertion amplification. The dream's current milestone isn't unresearched territory — it's territory I researched and never acted on.

Stopping here. No task files written, nothing implemented.
